  \"score\": 0.228,\n      \"title\": \"Feature Request: Add Table.title alignment\",\n      \"state\": \"closed\",\n      \"state_reason\": \"completed\",\n      \"strong\": false,\n      \"excerpt\": \"Have you checked the issues for a similar suggestions? Yes **How would you improve Rich?** Please add a table title alignment option. As I read the code the title is hardcoded to \\\"center\\\" **What problem does it solved for you?** User readability, having the table title left-aligned is a desired user-experience.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 3820,\n      \"score\": 0.22,\n      \"title\": \"[BUG] Panel does not honor expand=False when it contains Columns\",\n      \"state\": \"open\",\n      \"state_reason\": null,\n      \"strong\": false,\n      \"excerpt\": \"- [X] I've checked [docs](https://rich.readthedocs.io/en/latest/introduction.html) and [closed issues](https://github.com/Textualize/rich/issues?q=is%3Aissue+is%3Aclosed) for possible solutions. - [X] I can't find my issue in the [FAQ](https://github.com/Textualize/rich/blob/master/FAQ.md). **Describe the bug** The Panel object has an optional argument `expand`. When this is `True` (the default), the panel takes up the entire terminal width. When set to `False`, the panel shrinks to the width of the content inside the panel. This works most of the time, but fails when the Panel contains a Colu ...\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 1318,\n      \"score\": 0.205,\n      \"title\": \"[REQUEST] Support emoji variation selectors\",\n      \"state\": \"closed\",\n      \"state_reason\": \"completed\",\n      \"strong\": false,\n      \"excerpt\": \"**How would you improve Rich?** Add support for [variation selectors](https://stackoverflow.com/questions/38100329/some-emojis-e-g-have-two-unicode-u-u2601-and-u-u2601-ufe0f-what-does). I have recently stated using `rich` and want to migrate from the [emoji package](https://pypi.org/project/emoji/). However, the `emoji` package lets me specify a `variant_type` when printing. This will then append a sequence after every emoji to ensure that the correct variation is printed. See the `emoji` package [code in action](https://github.com/carpedm20/emoji/blob/70e7ba12dfaf3449a5d445b1e7de4ae2c6245d19/ ...\"\n    }\n  ]\n}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5aaa88ce-b3c1-40c0-8b34-15346b0c79e5","uuid":"9a890a26-55f1-4558-80f6-8b29e5bb8fb7","timestamp":"2026-10-27T08:02:41.332Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"{\n  \"searched_issues\": 1537,\n  \"quarantined\": 0,\n  \"threshold\": 0.35,\n  \"candidates\": [\n    {\n      \"number\": 3117,\n      \"score\": 0.261,\n      \"title\": \"[BUG] Panel inside Layout being cut off\",\n      \"state\": \"closed\",\n      \"state_reason\": \"completed\",\n      \"strong\": false,\n      \"excerpt\": \"- [x] I've checked [docs](https://rich.readthedocs.io/en/latest/introduction.html) and [closed issues](https://github.com/Textualize/rich/issues?q=is%3Aissue+is%3Aclosed) for possible solutions. - [x] I can't find my issue in the [FAQ](https://github.com/Textualize/rich/blob/master/FAQ.md). **Describe the bug** When rendering a panel inside a layout the content of the panel is cut short. The bottom border of the panel is still drawen. When printing the panel itself everything appears good. Note below render group can be replaced with a big string that would take up a lot of the terminal ```pyt ...\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 3520,\n      \"score\": 0.238,\n      \"title\": \"[REQUEST] Strip emoji shortcodes on emoji=False\",\n      \"state\": \"open\",\n      \"state_reason\": null,\n      \"strong\": false,\n      \"excerpt\": \"Have you checked the issues for a similar suggestions? Yes **How would you improve Rich?** Propose on Console to strip emoji (strip shortcodes before rendering) if emoji is False. Also add an options to if the user want to strip emoji or keep the emoji. Here this the code inherit from Console that strip emoji if emoji is False: ```pyt